{
  "id": "30558_iisoeru",
  "headword": "{言|い}い{添|そ}える",
  "reading": "いいそえる",
  "romaji": "iisoeru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan, transitive)",
  "gloss": "to add a remark; to say in addition",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to add a remark; to say in addition",
      "explanation": "To tack a short extra comment onto what one has just said, often a qualification, a reassurance, or a polite afterthought. The added remark is typically brief."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30558_iisoeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{一言|ひとこと}{言|い}い{添|そ}えた。",
      "english": "I added a word.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30558_iisoeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "「{無理|むり}はしないで」と{母|はは}は{言|い}い{添|そ}えた。",
      "english": "\"Don't push yourself,\" my mother added.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30558_iisoeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{説明|せつめい}の{最後|さいご}に、{彼|かれ}は「あくまで{現時点|げんじてん}での{予定|よてい}です」と{言|い}い{添|そ}えた。",
      "english": "At the end of his explanation, he added, \"This is only the plan as of now.\"",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A compound of {言|い}う (to say) and {添|そ}える (to attach, to accompany). Slightly literary; very common in narration and news writing to introduce a speaker's closing remark.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を for the words added, or a quoted remark with と\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {一言|ひとこと}{言|い}い{添|そ}える: to add a word\n- 〜と{言|い}い{添|そ}える: to add, \"~\"\n- {最後|さいご}に{言|い}い{添|そ}える: to add at the end\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {付|つ}け{加|くわ}える: to add — broader; works for information, conditions, or objects, not just speech\n- {付|つ}け{足|た}す: to tack on — plainer and more casual",
